---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const mail = `mailto:${site.contactEmail}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support"
  description="Help with TossLess: how food dates work, daily reminders, TossLess Pro purchases, subscriptions, refunds and where your data is stored."
>
  <div class="wrap page prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="summary">
      Need help? Most answers are below. If yours isn't, email <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a> and include your iPhone model and iOS version.
      We usually reply within a few days.
    </p>

    <h2>Using TossLess</h2>

    <h3>How does TossLess know when food goes bad?</h3>
    <p>
      When you add a food, TossLess suggests a use-by date based on how long that food usually keeps in the fridge, freezer or pantry. The guidance
      comes from the USDA FoodKeeper. Cooked leftovers are given 3 days. If the package has a printed date, tap “Pick date” and enter it: your date
      always wins over the estimate.
    </p>

    <h3>Are the dates and food guides safe to rely on?</h3>
    <p>
      They are estimates to help you plan, not a guarantee. Food can spoil sooner if it was stored warm, opened, or handled a lot. Always check the
      look, smell and texture, and follow the date on the package. When in doubt, throw it out.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I mark food as eaten, frozen or tossed?</h3>
    <p>
      On the Home screen, swipe a food to the left, or tap it to open its details. “Freeze it” moves it to the freezer and gives it a new date.
    </p>

    <h3>A barcode wasn't found</h3>
    <p>
      Product names come from Open Food Facts, a free database that doesn't know every product. If a barcode isn't found, type the name and pick a
      category, and we'll estimate the date. Barcode lookups also need an internet connection. Without one, you can still add the food by typing it.
    </p>

    <h2>Reminders</h2>

    <h3>I'm not getting the daily reminder</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Check that notifications are on: iOS Settings › TossLess › Notifications.</li>
      <li>In TossLess, go to Settings › Daily reminder and check the time.</li>
      <li>
        By default, the reminder is skipped on days when nothing is expiring. You can change this with “Skip reminder when nothing is expiring”.
      </li>
      <li>Open TossLess once in a while. Reminders are planned a week ahead and refreshed each time you open the app.</li>
      <li>Focus modes and Do Not Disturb can hide notifications.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>TossLess Pro and purchases</h2>

    <h3>What does Pro include?</h3>
    <p>
      Unlimited items (the free plan holds 20 at a time), Stats with money saved and what you toss most, and recipes from what's expiring.
    </p>

    <h3>I bought Pro but it isn't active</h3>
    <p>
      Open TossLess › Settings › Restore purchases while signed in with the same Apple ID you used to buy it. Make sure you have an internet
      connection.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I cancel my subscription?</h3>
    <p>
      Subscriptions are managed by Apple. On your iPhone, open Settings, tap your name, then Subscriptions › TossLess, and choose Cancel Subscription.
      Pro stays active until the end of the period you've paid for. Deleting the app doesn't cancel a subscription.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I get a refund?</h3>
    <p>Refunds are handled by Apple, not by us. Request one at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</p>

    <h3>Does the free trial cost anything?</h3>
    <p>
      The yearly plan may include a free trial. You won't be charged if you cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends. Your iPhone shows the
      exact trial length and price before you confirm.
    </p>

    <h2>Your data</h2>

    <h3>Where is my food list stored? Can I use it on another device?</h3>
    <p>
      Your list is stored only on your iPhone. There is no account and no sync between devices yet. Deleting the app deletes your list. Read more in
      the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .summary {
    background: var(--primary-tint);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1rem;
  }
  h2 {
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
